NETWORK USE
-----------

Section 13 of the AGPL applies to this software. If you run a modified version
and let users interact with it over a network, those users must be able to
obtain the corresponding source of your modified version.

This server implements its side of that obligation. Every HTTP response carries
an `X-Source-Code` header, and `GET /rest/v2/ping` (no authentication required)
reports the running version, revision and source URL:

    curl -sI https://your-host/ | grep -i x-source-code
    curl -s  https://your-host/rest/v2/ping

If you deploy a modified version, repoint these at the repository that publishes
your changes. Set `CANVAS_SOURCE_URL`, and set `CANVAS_SOURCE_COMMIT` where the
build has no git metadata, as in the container image. Removing the notice
instead of repointing it does not satisfy the licence.


