COMPONENTS
----------

Canvas is assembled from several repositories. They are not all licensed the
same way. Every component is available under the AGPL-3.0-or-later; only those
marked [dual] are also available under a commercial licence. Components in
separate repositories each carry their own LICENSE and NOTICE.

The server runtime and the services behind it, together the engine:

    [dual]  canvas-server   this repository, server runtime, transports, core
              src/services/embedd     embedding service
              src/services/messaging  notification and chat channels
              src/services/voice      speech-to-text and text-to-speech
              src/core/agent          agent runtime
    [dual]  canvas-synapsd  (dependency) context indexing engine
    [dual]  canvas-stored   (dependency) blob storage
    [dual]  canvas-inferd   (dependency) inference service
    [dual]  canvas-agentd   (repository) agent runtime service, consolidating
                            the former canvas-neurald

The clients, integrations and shared packages, AGPL-only for everyone. Most
live in the Canvas monorepo, https://github.com/canvas-ui/canvas:

    [AGPL]  apps/cli               (monorepo) command-line client
    [AGPL]  apps/web               (monorepo) web UI, served by this server
    [AGPL]  apps/shell             (monorepo) shell client and applets
    [AGPL]  apps/desktop           (monorepo) desktop app
    [AGPL]  apps/browser-extension (monorepo) Chrome and Firefox extensions
    [AGPL]  packages/*             (monorepo) protocol, schemas, api-client
    [AGPL]  canvas-fuse            (repository) FUSE filesystem client

A commercial licence to a [dual] component grants no rights over an [AGPL] one.
If you hold a commercial licence to the server runtime and you modify and convey
the CLI, the AGPL applies to that CLI in full. The same holds for the web UI:
it is AGPL-only, and serving a modified web UI to users over a network obliges
you to offer them its corresponding source, whatever engine licence you hold.


